<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fifth Syrian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">202–198 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fifth Syrian War, fought in 202–198 BCE, was a conflict between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> and the Ptolemaic kingdom. Antiochus's victory at Panium gave the Seleucids control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coele-syria">Coele-Syria</a>, including Judea, ending a century of Ptolemaic rule there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fifth-syrian-war.jpg" alt="Fifth Syrian War" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA, earthobservatory, http://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Near_east_lrg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
